IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc32-nif-xxi1`

-- ccc32-tests-nif-xxi1.l4 -- tests for ccc32-nif-xxi1.l4 (Part XXI.1 as replaced by 2024 c. 33 s. 3, with ss 5 and 6; NOT IN FORCE).
-- Every expected value is decided by reading the provision, and written beside the assertion. A failing assertion is a finding.
-- A DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable binary: each regulative rule is run with #TRACE (read the result: FULFILLED) and has a decision twin that is asserted.

§ `Section 3 and section 696.1`
#ASSERT `2024 c 33 s 3 Part XXI.1 is replaced by the following` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2024 c 33 s 3 Part XXI.1 is replaced by the following` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.1 (not in force) the definitions apply in the provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.1 (not in force) the definitions apply in the provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the three defined terms are "means" definitions: outside them the text says no.
#ASSERT `s 696.1 "applicant" (not in force)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.1 "applicant" (not in force)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.1 "Commission" (not in force)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.1 "Commission" (not in force)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.1 "court of appeal" (not in force)` Ontario Ontario EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.1 "court of appeal" (not in force)` Nunavut Nunavut EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.1 "court of appeal" (not in force)` Ontario Quebec EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.1 "court of appeal" (not in force)` `Nova Scotia` `New Brunswick` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 696.2 -- who may apply`
#ASSERT `s 696.2(1) (not in force) an application for a review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Commission by or on behalf of the person` `s 696.2(1)(a) (not in force) a person who has been found guilty of an offence under an Act of Parliament or a regulation made under an Act of Parliament` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.2(1) (not in force) an application for a review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Commission by or on behalf of the person` `s 696.2(1)(a) (not in force) a person found guilty under the Youth Criminal Justice Act or the Young Offenders Act, chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.2(1) (not in force) an application for a review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Commission by or on behalf of the person` `s 696.2(1)(a) (not in force) a person whose plea of guilty has been accepted` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.2(1) (not in force) an application for a review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Commission by or on behalf of the person` `s 696.2(1)(a) (not in force) a person who has been discharged under section 730` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.2(1) (not in force) an application for a review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Commission by or on behalf of the person` `s 696.2(1)(b) (not in force) a person who has been found to be a dangerous offender or long-term offender under Part XXIV` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.2(1) (not in force) an application for a review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Commission by or on behalf of the person` `s 696.2(1)(c) (not in force) a person who has been the subject of a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder under section 672.34` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a person the subsection does not name: not covered here (section 696.4(2) is what makes the Commission dismiss); an application not made by or for the person: outside the wording.
#ASSERT `s 696.2(1) (not in force) an application for a review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Commission by or on behalf of the person` `s 696.2(1) (not in force) a person of another kind` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.2(1) (not in force) an application for a review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Commission by or on behalf of the person` `s 696.2(1)(a) (not in force) a person who has been found guilty of an offence under an Act of Parliament or a regulation made under an Act of Parliament` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): the application must say whether appeal rights are exhausted and, if not, give information on the section 696.4(4) factors.
#ASSERT `s 696.2(2) (not in force) the application includes what it must include` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.2(2) (not in force) the application includes what it must include` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.2(2) (not in force) the application includes what it must include` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.2(2) (not in force) the application includes what it must include` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 696.3`
#TRACE `s 696.3(1) (not in force) the Commission must deal with the application as expeditiously as possible` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` DOES `s 696.3(1) (not in force) deal with the application as expeditiously as possible` AT 1

#TRACE `s 696.3(1) (not in force) the Commission must provide the applicant with an update on a regular basis` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` DOES `s 696.3(1) (not in force) provide the applicant with an update concerning the status of their application on a regular basis` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 696.3(1) (not in force) the Commission owes the applicant the duty to deal with the application as expeditiously as possible and to provide regular updates` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.3(1) (not in force) the Commission owes the applicant the duty to deal with the application as expeditiously as possible and to provide regular updates` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.3(2) (not in force) the notice or information may be provided to a representative of the applicant in addition to or instead of the applicant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.3(2) (not in force) the notice or information may be provided to a representative of the applicant in addition to or instead of the applicant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.3(2) (not in force) the notice or information may be provided to a representative of the applicant in addition to or instead of the applicant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 696.4 -- admissibility`
#TRACE `s 696.4(1) (not in force) the Commission must decide whether the application is admissible` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` DOES `s 696.4(1) (not in force) decide whether the application is admissible` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 696.4(1) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to decide whether the application is admissible` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(1) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to decide whether the application is admissible` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.4(2) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application as inadmissible on the ground that the person is not described in subsection 696.2(1)` `s 696.2(1) (not in force) a person of another kind` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(2) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application as inadmissible on the ground that the person is not described in subsection 696.2(1)` `s 696.2(1)(a) (not in force) a person who has been found guilty of an offence under an Act of Parliament or a regulation made under an Act of Parliament` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(2) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application as inadmissible on the ground that the person is not described in subsection 696.2(1)` `s 696.2(1)(a) (not in force) a person found guilty under the Youth Criminal Justice Act or the Young Offenders Act, chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(2) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application as inadmissible on the ground that the person is not described in subsection 696.2(1)` `s 696.2(1)(a) (not in force) a person whose plea of guilty has been accepted` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(2) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application as inadmissible on the ground that the person is not described in subsection 696.2(1)` `s 696.2(1)(a) (not in force) a person who has been discharged under section 730` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(2) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application as inadmissible on the ground that the person is not described in subsection 696.2(1)` `s 696.2(1)(b) (not in force) a person who has been found to be a dangerous offender or long-term offender under Part XXIV` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(2) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application as inadmissible on the ground that the person is not described in subsection 696.2(1)` `s 696.2(1)(c) (not in force) a person who has been the subject of a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder under section 672.34` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(3) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application as inadmissible on a ground in subsection (3)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(3) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application as inadmissible on a ground in subsection (3)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(3) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application as inadmissible on a ground in subsection (3)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(3) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application as inadmissible on a ground in subsection (3)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4) (not in force) the Commission may decide that the application is admissible despite subsection (3)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4) (not in force) the Commission may decide that the application is admissible despite subsection (3)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.4(4)(a) (not in force) the amount of time that has passed since the final judgment of the trial court` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.4(4)(b) (not in force) the reasons why the finding or verdict was not appealed to the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.4(4)(c) (not in force) whether it would serve a useful purpose for an application to be made for an extension of the period within which a notice of appeal or a notice of application for leave to appeal, as the case may be, to the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada may be served and filed` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.4(4)(d) (not in force) whether the application is supported by a new matter of significance` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.4(4)(e) (not in force) any other factor that it considers relevant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.4(4)(e) (not in force) any other factor that it considers relevant` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4)(d) (not in force) the application is supported by a new matter of significance that meets subparagraphs (i) to (iii)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4)(d) (not in force) the application is supported by a new matter of significance that meets subparagraphs (i) to (iii)` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4)(d) (not in force) the application is supported by a new matter of significance that meets subparagraphs (i) to (iii)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4)(d) (not in force) the application is supported by a new matter of significance that meets subparagraphs (i) to (iii)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.4(4)(d) (not in force) the application is supported by a new matter of significance that meets subparagraphs (i) to (iii)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 696.4(5) (not in force) the Commission must notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision on admissibility` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` DOES `s 696.4(5) (not in force) notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision regarding the admissibility of the application` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 696.4(5) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision on admissibility` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4(5) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision on admissibility` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 696.5 -- investigation`
#ASSERT `s 696.5(1) (not in force) the Commission may conduct an investigation in relation to the application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(1) (not in force) the Commission may conduct an investigation in relation to the application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(1) (not in force) the Commission may conduct an investigation in relation to the application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 696.5(1) (not in force) the Commission may conduct an investigation in relation to the application` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a power and its failed "if" gate is the text's limit on the grant, not the text's no, so the answer is NOTHING (name-test sweep, fork F24)
#ASSERT `s 696.5(1) (not in force) the Commission may conduct an investigation in relation to the application` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 696.5(2) (not in force) the Commission must send a notice indicating whether an investigation will be conducted` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` DOES `s 696.5(2) (not in force) send a notice to the applicant and to the relevant Attorney General indicating whether an investigation will be conducted` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 696.5(2) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to send a notice indicating whether an investigation will be conducted` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(2) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to send a notice indicating whether an investigation will be conducted` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.5(2) (not in force) the notice must also specify a reasonable period within which further information may be provided` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(2) (not in force) the notice must also specify a reasonable period within which further information may be provided` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(3) (not in force) the condition for deciding under section 696.6 without an investigation is met` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(3) (not in force) the condition for deciding under section 696.6 without an investigation is met` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(4) (not in force) the Commission has the powers of a commissioner under Part I of the Inquiries Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(4) (not in force) the Commission has the powers of a commissioner under Part I of the Inquiries Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.5(5) (not in force) the Commission may authorize the person to exercise the powers referred to in subsection (4)` `s 696.5(5) (not in force) an employee of the Commission` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(5) (not in force) the Commission may authorize the person to exercise the powers referred to in subsection (4)` `s 696.5(5) (not in force) a person under contract to the Commission who has technical or specialized knowledge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(5) (not in force) the Commission may authorize the person to exercise the powers referred to in subsection (4)` `s 696.5(5) (not in force) a person of another kind` EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 696.5(6) (not in force) the Commission must prepare a report and provide a copy of it` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` DOES `s 696.5(6) (not in force) prepare a report and provide a copy of it to the applicant and the relevant Attorney General` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 696.5(6) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to prepare a report and provide a copy of it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(6) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to prepare a report and provide a copy of it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.5(7) (not in force) the report must specify a reasonable period within which a written response may be provided` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(7) (not in force) the report must specify a reasonable period within which a written response may be provided` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (8) "only if": responses or confirmation received in the period, or the period has ended; otherwise the text's no.
#ASSERT `s 696.5(8) (not in force) the condition for deciding under section 696.6 after an investigation is met` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(8) (not in force) the condition for deciding under section 696.6 after an investigation is met` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(8) (not in force) the condition for deciding under section 696.6 after an investigation is met` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.5(8) (not in force) the condition for deciding under section 696.6 after an investigation is met` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 696.6 -- decision and remedies`
#TRACE `s 696.6(1) (not in force) the Commission must make a decision on the application` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` DOES `s 696.6(1) (not in force) make a decision on the application` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 696.6(1) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to make a decision on the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(1) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to make a decision on the application` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.6(2) (not in force) the Commission must grant a remedy under paragraph (a) or (b)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(2) (not in force) the Commission must grant a remedy under paragraph (a) or (b)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(2) (not in force) the Commission must grant a remedy under paragraph (a) or (b)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(2) (not in force) the Commission must grant a remedy under paragraph (a) or (b)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) the form of the new proceeding the Commission directs` TRUE EQUALS `s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) a new hearing under Part XXIV`
#ASSERT `s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) the form of the new proceeding the Commission directs` FALSE EQUALS `s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) a new trial before any court that the Commission thinks proper`
#ASSERT `s 696.6(3) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(3) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(4) (not in force) the Commission may take the step` TRUE `s 696.6(4) (not in force) refer the matter to the court of appeal under paragraph (2)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(4) (not in force) the Commission may take the step` TRUE `s 696.6(4) (not in force) dismiss the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(4) (not in force) the Commission may take the step` TRUE `s 696.6(4) (not in force) direct a new trial or a new hearing under paragraph (2)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(4) (not in force) the Commission may take the step` FALSE `s 696.6(4) (not in force) refer the matter to the court of appeal under paragraph (2)(b)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.6(5) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.6(5)(a) (not in force) whether the application is supported by a new matter of significance that was not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Commission in an application in relation to the same finding or verdict` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(5) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.6(5)(b) (not in force) the relevance and reliability of the information that is presented in connection with the application` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(5) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.6(5)(c) (not in force) the fact that an application is not intended to serve as a further appeal and that the remedies set out in subsection (2) are extraordinary remedies` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(5) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.6(5)(d) (not in force) the personal circumstances of the applicant` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(5) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.6(5)(e) (not in force) the distinct challenges that applicants who belong to certain populations face in obtaining a remedy for a miscarriage of justice, with particular attention to the circumstances of Indigenous or Black applicants` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(5) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.6(5)(f) (not in force) any other factor that it considers relevant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(5) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` `s 696.6(5)(f) (not in force) any other factor that it considers relevant` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.6(6) (not in force) the Commission may grant a remedy under subsection (2) even if the evidence does not establish the innocence of the applicant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(6) (not in force) the Commission may grant a remedy under subsection (2) even if the evidence does not establish the innocence of the applicant` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 696.6(7) (not in force) the Commission must notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` DOES `s 696.6(7) (not in force) notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 696.6(7) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.6(7) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 696.61, section 696.7 and section 696.72`
#ASSERT `s 696.61 (not in force) the Commission may refer the question to the court of appeal for its opinion` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.61 (not in force) the Commission may refer the question to the court of appeal for its opinion` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.61 (not in force) the Commission may refer the question to the court of appeal for its opinion` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
